Suggests: yt-dlp
Description: retro terminal music player inspired by Winamp 2.x
 cliamp is a terminal music player with a Winamp-inspired interface: a
 playlist editor, a graphic equaliser, dozens of visualisers and a large
 collection of themes, all rendered in the terminal.
 .
 It plays local files (MP3, FLAC, OGG, WAV) and internet radio, and can
 stream from Spotify, Qobuz, Navidrome, Jellyfin, Emby, Plex, SoundCloud,
 NetEase and YouTube Music. A headless daemon mode exposes playback over
 IPC for scripts, Waybar and other status bars, and playback can be
 extended with sandboxed Lua plugins.
 .
 The command provided by this package is "cliamp".
